{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2165-06-28 18:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2165-06-28 18:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve been having this pressure in my left tricep and forearm. It started yesterday afternoon. It’s not chest pain, but I know this feeling—it’s how my heart problems started before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2165-06-28 18:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you’ve had this kind of pain before, linked to heart issues?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2165-06-28 18:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, before my bypass surgery years ago. I had left arm pain just like this, and it turned out to be a heart attack. I didn’t have chest pain then either. This feels very similar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2165-06-28 18:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. Did you take anything for the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2165-06-28 18:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I took four baby aspirins last night. The pain got better, and I slept okay. But when I woke up this morning, it was back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2165-06-28 18:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Any shortness of breath, nausea, or sweating?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2165-06-28 18:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, none of that. But I’ve been feeling really anxious today. It’s the anniversary of my mother’s death. I’ve been tearful all day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2165-06-28 18:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m so sorry. That makes sense. We’ll keep that in mind. We’ve checked your vital signs and did some blood work. Your heart enzymes are normal, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2165-06-28 18:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not a heart attack?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2165-06-28 18:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not based on the blood tests. But because this pain is your anginal equivalent, we want to be thorough. We’ve scheduled a stress test for tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2165-06-28 18:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes me feel better. I just didn’t want to ignore it again like last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2165-06-28 18:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did the right thing coming in. We’ll also do an echocardiogram to check your heart function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2165-06-29 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your echo was done yesterday. The heart’s pumping function is strong—ejection fraction is about 75%. But the images were a bit hard to read, so we can’t rule out a small wall motion issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2165-06-29 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So is my heart okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2165-06-29 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Overall, yes. But we still need to understand the cause of your arm pain. Your stress test results are back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2165-06-29 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2165-06-29 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You didn’t have any chest pain or EKG changes during the test. The nuclear images show slightly irregular perfusion in the inferior part of the heart, but it might be due to body tissue blocking the view. No definite blockage was seen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2165-06-29 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So is it my heart or not?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2165-06-29 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s still concerning enough that we recommend a cardiac catheterization. It’s the best way to see if there’s a blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2165-06-29 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will they put in a stent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2165-06-29 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see what we find. If there’s a significant blockage, we may do an angioplasty to open it. But we won’t know until we look inside."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2165-06-30 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back from the cath lab. The procedure went well. We found a 90% blockage in a branch of your left circumflex artery. It wasn’t covered by your bypass graft."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2165-06-30 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. Did you put in a stent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2165-06-30 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an angioplasty—used a balloon to open the artery. But we didn’t place a stent. The vessel opened well, and blood flow is now good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2165-06-30 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m fixed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2165-06-30 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The blockage is opened, yes. But we also found that you have three-vessel coronary disease, which means your heart arteries are generally narrowed. Your heart’s squeezing function is still strong."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2165-06-30 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I’ve had this pain before and they said it wasn’t my heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2165-06-30 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s true. And today, after the procedure, you had some arm pain again for a few minutes. But it resolved on its own. We think it’s unlikely to be from heart ischemia now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2165-06-30 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s causing it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2165-06-30 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could still be heart-related, given your history. But it might also be musculoskeletal or related to anxiety. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2165-06-30 14:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been seeing an acupuncturist for anxiety. Should I keep doing that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2165-06-30 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s fine. We didn’t start any new anxiety medication because of your recent heart procedure, but we recommend discussing an SSRI with your doctor as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2165-07-01 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’ve been pain-free overnight, and your vitals are stable. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2165-07-01 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What do I need to do when I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2165-07-01 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take a full-dose aspirin—325 mg daily—instead of the baby aspirin. And your Toprol dose is being increased to 50 mg once a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2165-07-01 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Why the change?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2165-07-01 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The higher beta-blocker dose helps reduce heart workload, especially with your known coronary disease. The full aspirin dose is standard after angioplasty."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2165-07-01 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2165-07-01 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your usual medications—atorvastatin, levothyroxine, calcium, and raloxifene. No changes there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2165-07-01 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2165-07-01 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have a cardiology follow-up in one week. Make sure to attend. And please don’t skip any future stress tests if recommended."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2165-07-01 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I won’t. I’ve learned my lesson."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2165-07-01 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did the right thing coming in. Even if the pain wasn’t from a new heart attack, we found and treated a serious blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2165-07-01 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better knowing that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2165-07-01 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You should be home within a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2165-07-01 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check before you leave. Any pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2165-07-01 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, none at all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2165-07-01 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Vitals are stable. You’re cleared to go home. Take care, and follow up as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2165-07-01 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I really appreciate everything."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2165-06-28 18:08:00",
    "admission_end": "2165-07-01 12:50:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 70-year-old woman with a history of coronary artery disease and prior CABG was admitted for left tricep and forearm pain, which she recognized as her anginal equivalent. She presented on the anniversary of her mother’s death and reported heightened anxiety. Initial evaluation showed normal cardiac enzymes and a normal chest X-ray. A stress test was non-diagnostic, with no ischemic changes, though nuclear imaging showed possible artifact-related perfusion irregularities. Cardiac catheterization revealed a 90% stenosis in the left circumflex artery, which was treated with percutaneous balloon angioplasty without stenting. The patient remained stable post-procedure, with resolution of symptoms. She was discharged home with increased metoprolol dose and aspirin 325 mg daily, with follow-up planned. Her arm pain after the procedure was brief and not deemed ischemic.",
    "problems": [
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of native coronary artery",
      "Other and unspecified angina pectoris",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism"
    ]
  }
}
